LLL -- compute an LLL basis
***************************

  * Usage: 
        LLL m
  * Inputs:
      * m, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, or a *note MutableMatrix:
        (Macaulay2Doc)MutableMatrix,, over *note ZZ: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, whose
        columns are linearly independent
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note ChangeMatrix: LLL_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmChangeMatrix=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value false, also find change of basis matrix
      * Limit (missing documentation) => ..., default value infinity, 
      * *note Strategy: LLL_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value NTL, choose among different algorithms
      * Threshold (missing documentation) => ..., default value null, 
  * Outputs:
      * A matrix or mutable matrix, respectively, whose columns form an LLL
        (Lenstra-Lenstra-Lovasz) basis of the image lattice of the matrix

Description
===========


This function is provided by the package *note LLLBases: Top,.  If the optional
argument ChangeMatrix=>true is given, then the output is a pair of matrices:
the first is the LLL matrix as above, and the second is the change of basis
matrix from the original basis to the new basis.


In this example, we compute the LLL basis of the nullspace of a matrix.  This
is an example of Havas et al.
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : m1 = map(ZZ^10, ZZ^10, (j,i) -> (i+1)^3 * (j+1)^2 + i + j + 2)  |
|                                                                     |
|o1 = | 3   11  31   69   131   223   351   521   739   1011   |      |
|     | 7   36  113  262  507   872   1381  2058  2927  4012   |      |
|     | 13  77  249  583  1133  1953  3097  4619  6573  9013   |      |
|     | 21  134 439  1032 2009  3466  5499  8204  11677 16014  |      |
|     | 31  207 683  1609 3135  5411  8587  12813 18239 25015  |      |
|     | 43  296 981  2314 4511  7788  12361 18446 26259 36016  |      |
|     | 57  401 1333 3147 6137  10597 16821 25103 35737 49017  |      |
|     | 73  522 1739 4108 8013  13838 21967 32784 46673 64018  |      |
|     | 91  659 2199 5197 10139 17511 27799 41489 59067 81019  |      |
|     | 111 812 2713 6414 12515 21616 34317 51218 72919 100020 |      |
|                                                                     |
|              10       10                                            |
|o1 : Matrix ZZ   <-- ZZ                                              |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : m = syz m1                                                      |
|                                                                     |
|o2 = | -3 -1632481 -2819632 -4476373  -6680969  -9511685  -13046786 ||
|     | 8  4353284  7519023  11937004  17815934  25364520  34791469  ||
|     | -7 -3809126 -6579152 -10444892 -15588965 -22193990 -30442586 ||
