LLL(...,ChangeMatrix=>...) -- also find change of basis matrix
**************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        (B,U) = LLL(A,ChangeMatrix=>true)
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, over the integers, of size d
        by n
  * Outputs:
      * B, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the LLL matrix (also having d
        rows)
      * U, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the n by n invertible
        transform matrix
  * Consequences:
      * The routine returns a pair of matrices, rather than just one

Description
===========

Constructs the change of basis matrix U from the basis A to the basis B. This
is an invertible matrix U such that$AU = B$.
